-- The Ace Tsar Molotov hookah (catalogue p26) shows the shop's own photos (Google Drive, 2026-11-27). Not applied live yet.
-- The shop's green and blue Tsar (IMG_0684, IMG_0685) stood on a patterned mat that showed through the clear glass base;
-- store/tools/catalog/clear_glass.py clears what is seen through the glass and keeps the glass's own outline and highlights.
--   OSS-100084 (green chip): shop/ace-tsar-molotov-green, its own photo (it showed the blue photo, "Shown in blue"); its colour
--     name becomes green, read off the photo (still "Colours TBD" until the shop confirms it).
--   OSS-100081 (blue chip): shop/ace-tsar-molotov-blue in place of the web photo.
--   OSS-100080, OSS-100083 (red and yellow chips, no photo of their own): still "Shown in blue", now on the shop's blue photo.
--   OSS-100150 (the Ace Rose, shop photo since shop-photos-2026-11-27.sql): its chip colour, measured from that photo.
-- Each shop photo's chip colour (photo_hex) is measured from the photo (photos.colour_of), as for the catalogue photos.
-- Only img, variant_label and the photo keys of facts_known (photo, photo_hex, photo_label, shown_in, photo_upscale) move,
-- set with json_set/json_remove: every other fact (the reverse-search and web facts) and the name stay as they are live.
-- A second run touches no row (each line only runs where a value still differs). Needs store/public/img/pc/shop/
-- ace-tsar-molotov-{green,blue}*.webp deployed with the same commit. The values are catalog.py's (store/catalog/suppliers/ace/
-- master.json); test_catalog.py checks they still match.
-- Run after shop-photos-2026-11-27.sql and never re-run that file after this one: its whole-string Rose line would match
-- again and drop the Rose's photo_hex. photo_src (the maker's page) is left as live on OSS-100081/84: it is not shown.
-- Rollback (the live values before this change, 2026-11-27):
